From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: karsyboy <karsyboy@k-ops.cloud>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:32:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] c-api: 1.1 additions for color metadata, overlay layers
 and completion

Upstream froze the C API/ABI at 1.0; these are additions on top of it,
so the library reports 1.1.0.

- pyrowave_encoder_set_color_metadata: the sequence header's color
  fields (primaries, transfer, matrix, range, siting) were always zero.
  They are now written at packetize time from the metadata current when
  the frame was encoded; the scaled path derives them from its color
  spaces and range.
- pyrowave_encoder_encode_gpu_scaled_overlay/_layers: composite up to
  two layers (CPU texels or an imported RGBA image, with opacity) over a
  single-plane RGB input, through the patched Granite scaler.
- Completion contract: Granite's fence wait reports nothing on failure,
  so the readback calls now check that the fence really signalled and
  return PYROWAVE_ERROR_GENERIC otherwise. A failed scaled encode waits
  for scaler work it already queued, so an error means no read of the
  caller's input is outstanding, except PYROWAVE_ERROR_GENERIC.
- packetize validates its arguments and that the encoded blocks fit the
  output before writing.
- The readback copy is reported as its own GPU stage.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
